I've written the plan for this session: two task files and the issue responses are in session_plan/. The commit failed because session_plan/ is gitignored, so the files exist on disk but aren't committed. The commit command ends in || true, so that looks expected.

Task 1, Part of #991 (prompt code, `product`): when yoyo -p writes to a pipe, wrap its events with yoagent's retry_safe_events. Today, if the connection drops after text has started and the retry would have worked, yoyo stops with an error and leaves the partial text. With the wrapper, a retry that succeeds prints its answer once and exits 0. Terminal output must not change at all. The cost is that piped text arrives one attempt at a time instead of word by word.
• The agent reads yoagent's retry code first, and also its rules for which errors get retried, before choosing the error the test server sends.
• Three tests check the exact output: a retry that works after partial text, a retry before any text (already passes; it guards against breaking that), and a run where every attempt fails.
• It fixes the comment in retry_after_partial.rs that describes #991 as future work. If the wrapper turns out not to fit this code path, the task records why on #991 instead of forcing a fix.
• The rest of #991 stays open: the leftover text in the streaming-JSON mode, and two untested edge cases.

Task 2, the Discussion #420 promise (`product`): add --no-hints and hints = false in .yoyo.toml to turn off the one-line tips the REPL prints after a turn. I promised this on Day 84 and never built it.
• Hints stay on by default, so nothing changes for anyone who doesn't set either option.
• The flag is documented in the same change. A project's own .yoyo.toml can only turn hints off, so it needs no trust check.
• The commit body notes that #420 is owed a reply, because a commit can't close a discussion.

